+### 4.3 list_sessions
+
+Asks for the connected user's conversations, so a client can offer a history list without a second, HTTP route over the same personal data. The answer is `session_list` (Section 5.9).
+
+```json
+{
+  "type": "list_sessions",
+  "limit": 10,
+  "before": { "updatedAt": "2026-01-01T00:05:00.000Z", "sessionId": "s3" }
+}
+```
+
+| Field               | Type            | Required | Description                                                                 |
+| ------------------- | --------------- | -------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
+| `type`              | string          | Yes      | `"list_sessions"`                                                           |
+| `limit`             | number          | No       | At most this many summaries, newest activity first                          |
+| `before`            | object          | No       | Resume after this row when paging: the last summary the client showed       |
+| `before.updatedAt`  | string\|number  | No       | That row's activity time, an ISO-8601 string or an epoch number             |
+| `before.sessionId`  | string          | No       | That row's session id, which breaks a tie between two equally active rows   |
+
+Whose list:
+
+- The user is the connection's own, read from the socket's authentication: the frame carries no user id the server would honour, and any `userId` a client sends is dropped by the validator, so a frame naming another user lists no one else ([validated by: answers list_sessions for the authenticated user with ISO dates, forwarding limit and before while ignoring any client userId](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L74), [validated by: answers list_sessions with the session user's own summaries, ISO dates, limit and before forwarded and a client userId ignored](../../src/transport/ws/messageHandler.test.ts#L873)).
+
+Constraints, each violation answered with `INVALID_MESSAGE` and no list asked of the store:
+
+- `limit`, when present, MUST be an integer of 0 or more.
+- `before`, when present, MUST be an object whose `sessionId` is a string of 1 to 128 characters and whose `updatedAt` parses as a timestamp, so a cursor that went through JSON still pages ([validated by: accepts a bare list_sessions frame and rejects a malformed limit or before with INVALID_MESSAGE without calling listFor](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L124), [validated by: accepts list_sessions with an integer limit and a before cursor, and rejects either malformed](../../src/transport/ws/validation.test.ts#L25)).
+
+Not a turn:
+
+- A `list_sessions` is answered beside `ping`, outside the per-session lock of Section 4.1: a history request mutates nothing and MUST NOT wait behind a streaming answer.
+- Answers given beside the lock are written one at a time per socket, in the order their frames arrived: a `list_sessions` answered in the same tick as a `ping` is written before that `pong`, so a client that asks and then heartbeats reads its list first ([validated by: answers a list_sessions asked in the same tick as a ping before that ping, in the order the frames arrived](../../src/transport/ws/messageHandler.test.ts#L899)).
